Here is a complete, self-contained CUDA program that measures genuine
co-residency of two concurrently launched kernels on the same SM. It records
per-CTA start/stop times from `%globaltimer` and the SM id from `%smid`, takes
the dynamic shared memory request as a launch parameter so occupancy can be
swept, runs on two non-blocking streams with no cross-stream event waits, and
post-processes to report the peak number of CTAs resident on any single SM
across both kernels.

